  "description": "PROCESS-PF7-KEY at :234-252 with CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM equal to one, so 'IF CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM > 1' at :245 is FALSE and PROCESS-PAGE-BACKWARD is never performed - no STARTBR, no READPREV, no ENDBR. TRANSACT is still seeded with twelve 350-byte rows, FILLER included, so that 'the browse never happened' is an assertion about a file that had something to read rather than a vacuous statement about an empty one. Reaching the paragraph is itself part of the branch, and it is ordered: :112 finds CDEMO-PGM-REENTER already true, :118 receives the map, and DFHPF7 is matched by the THIRD of the five EVALUATE EIBAID arms at :125-126 - after DFHENTER and DFHPF3, before DFHPF8 and WHEN OTHER - so the position of the test is as much the behaviour as the test is. What the paragraph does before the page comparison is still observable and is pinned here: TRAN-ID is set from CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST at :239 and, crucially, SET NEXT-PAGE-YES at :242 runs UNCONDITIONALLY - so the flag comes back Y even though nothing was paged and the inbound flag was N. That makes this the only case that arrives at Y by CHANGING the flag rather than echoing it, which is why its response shape coincides with case10's while its inbound state and its message do not. The screen is re-sent WITHOUT ERASE (:250 SET SEND-ERASE-NO, then the single PERFORM SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN at :251) so the rows the terminal echoed stay on the display, and the message is 'You are already at the top of the page...' - which is a different literal from the 'You are at the top of the page...' STARTBR uses at :608-609 and from the 'You have reached the top of the page...' READPREV uses at :676-677. The mandated class name is TransactionMenuController and is honoured verbatim, but the program LISTS transactions - README:L221 records CT00 / COTRN00 / COTRN00C as 'Transaction List' - and every value below is taken from the paired source, never from the name. Statically derived: read out of app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl and cross-